   "id": "korea-swing",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "KOSPI gives back 3% after Wednesday’s 6.6% jump as Samsung’s quarter falls short",
   "when": "Wed 28 Oct to Thu 11:20 KST",
   "what": "The KOSPI closed Wednesday at 6,012.44, up 6.63%, after SK hynix posted record quarterly revenue of ₩104.6 trillion and a 2026 shareholder-return plan worth more than ₩100 trillion. On Thursday it was down 3.0% by late morning after Samsung’s third-quarter results came in slightly below forecasts and its shares fell 6.6%; SK hynix edged up 0.4%.",
   "why": "Korea is your largest exposure. Your dashboard still prices SCBKEQTG at its 26 Oct NAV, and the KOSPI is about 7% above that close even after today’s drop, so most of this week’s gain isn’t in your portfolio value yet. EWY, which you hold directly, rose 5.4% in New York on Wednesday.",
