   "headline": "Fed holds at 3.75–4.00%; two officials voted for a hike",
   "when": "Wed 28 Oct · 14:00 ET",
   "what": "The FOMC voted 10–2 to leave its target range unchanged. Governor Lisa Cook and Cleveland Fed President Beth Hammack wanted a quarter-point increase. The statement described inflation as elevated and growth as strong. The Fed raised rates in September for the first time since 2023.",
