   "headline": "Alphabet misses on revenue and profit; its shares fall about 10% after hours",
   "when": "Wed 28 Oct · after the US close",
   "what": "Third-quarter revenue was $127.6 billion against $128.2 billion expected, and Search revenue of $63.4 billion also fell short. Cloud revenue doubled, but free cash flow turned negative at $9.1 billion as capital spending reached $51.4 billion. Analysts quoted by CNBC called it the first miss on both revenue and earnings in nearly four years.",
